{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1088193-craft-science-and-specialties","id":1088193,"title":"Craft...Science...and Specialties?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-05T04:26:57-07:00","id":1088193,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Craft...Science...and Specialties?","content":"Okay so I am at a real crossroads. I am pondering what Craft/Science/Specialties rules to use? As written it really sounds like you can only be good at one type of Craft or Science, and generally well at others.<br /> <br /> I was contemplating a few ways to handle this. I could just go as is, but I don't want that. I could have it they learn a separate Craft/Science for each area of Expertise like in Exalted, I don't mind this, I mean Crafts and Sciences are dramatic and what people use to build the World. Or I could allow them to add extra Specialties to represent being like Reed Richards and mastering various fields of insane Science and Engineering, this may be a groovy option too, but how much should I charge for this?<br /> <br /> <br /> Please I would be very interested in getting as many opinions on this as possible so I can weigh my options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T05:14:34-07:00","id":1088212,"title":"","content":"Most types of crafting and also all fields of science have some cross-refrences to other crafts/sciences. As a biologist, you have to have knowledge about chemicals and physics, but also might need some knowledge about psychology of animals and you might want to know some latin and greek, some things about medicine and so on. What are your points against or for any 'system' you want to use?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T08:31:00-07:00","id":1088305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheVarulfen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1088193-craft-science-and-specialties?p=1088212#post1088212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most types of crafting and also all fields of science have some cross-refrences to other crafts/sciences. As a biologist, you have to have knowledge about chemicals and physics, but also might need some knowledge about psychology of animals and you might want to know some latin and greek, some things about medicine and so on. What are your points against or for any 'system' you want to use?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actual Latin and Greek tend to be pretty divorced from the words borrowed to describe anatomy and such. No one's going to really learn to speak either from their time studying biology; typically, it just increases your vocabulary slightly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T12:12:24-07:00","id":1088408,"title":"","content":"I prefer the M20 &quot;Well-Skilled Craftsman&quot; optional rule.<br /> <br /> The basic idea is that some Abilities that have a lot of broad subdivisions (V20 has a list like this too) let you select a Specialty at the first dot, and at the fourth dot you can buy additional Specialties for 4 XP","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T11:55:05-07:00","id":1089288,"title":"","content":"This is one of those areas where I kind of liked the 1st ed Exalted approach. If you were, say, an MD, you could take Science 2 and add two Specialty dots of Biology on top of it. <br /> <br /> (I've not seen M20, but the Well-Skilled Craftsman rule seems like a good idea also.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}